<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jizan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jazan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jizan is a port city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> in south-western Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> and the capital of Jizan Province. It was part of the Idrisid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asir">Asir</a> in the early 20th century and came under Saudi rule in the 1930s. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>'s claim to the area was given up in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-taif">Treaty of Ta'if</a> of 1934, after the Saudi-Yemeni war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jizan.jpg" alt="Jizan" width="320" height="272" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AliAlghamdi12 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jizan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
